{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggeEUYrmrNnoYwbzWfNy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dq ≈ 427 cm⁻¹ (Δt ≈ 4 270 cm⁻¹) and B ≈ 899 cm⁻¹. C is not determined.\n\n**Method.** A d⁸ ion in a tetrahedral field has the same term pattern as an octahedral d² ion. The ground term is ³T₁(F). The three spin-allowed bands are:\n- ν₁ = ³T₁(F) → ³T₂, at 3 600 cm⁻¹.\n- ν₂ = ³T₁(F) → ³A₂, at 7 870 cm⁻¹.\n- ν₃ = ³T₁(F) → ³T₁(P), at 16 410 cm⁻¹.\n\nWithout configuration mixing, ν₂/ν₁ would be 18Dq/8Dq = 2.25. The observed ratio is 2.19. This difference comes from mixing of the two ³T₁ terms, so I fitted all three bands with the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices rather than the simple formulas.\n\n**Fit.** I used the ts_fit_spectrum tool with the d² (octahedral-equivalent) manifold. It reproduced the bands to within 2 cm⁻¹ (RMSE about 1.2 cm⁻¹):\n\n| Band | Observed (cm⁻¹) | Calculated (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ν₁ | 3 600 | 3 598 |\n| ν₂ | 7 870 | 7 871 |\n| ν₃ | 16 410 | 16 410 |\n\nThe fitted B is about 899 cm⁻¹. The free-ion value for Ni²⁺ is roughly 1 040 cm⁻¹, so B/B₀ ≈ 0.86.\n\n**C.** The spin-allowed bands do not depend on C. The tool's 3 801 cm⁻¹ is only a default carried through the fit, so I am not reporting C as a result.\n\n{\"Dq\": 427, \"B\": 899, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Three spin-allowed bands of tetrahedral d8 fit to Dq and B by the Tanabe-Sugano matrices; C is not constrained by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1837,"cache_read_input_tokens":7975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1837,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bd8fa11-b86f-4004-ba6b-